title: Duplicates
kind: overview
aliases: duplicate identical reclaimable
summary: Find the files holding byte-identical content, recorded as duplicate groups you query like any other metadata.

A ''duplicate scan'' finds the files of a repository whose contents are
byte-identical, and records each set as a ''duplicate group'': a metarecord of
its own, which every member file points at. It reports only a summary. Which
files have a twin, which groups waste the most space, what else is identical to
this file: those are ordinary queries over the fields the scan wrote — which is
why it writes them.

Nothing here deletes or moves a file. Disposing of a copy is your act, and goes
through the [[Trash]].

